      "card_ids": ["C17","C11","C04","C12","C08","C07"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 absorption records for related basic amines show high intestinal absorption: imipramine human Fa ~100% and essentially complete absorption (C101, C104, C132, C150) with high passive permeability and low efflux (C145); PNU-96391 >90% GI absorption in rats (C133); procainamide 75-100% GI absorption (C102, C144, C146).",
      "card_ids": ["C101","C104","C132","C150","C145","C133","C102","C144","C146"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 gut-wall/efflux records for related basic amines show high Caco-2 permeability and low/no significant efflux: imipramine Papp A-B 10.8 x 10^-6 cm/s with efflux ratio 1.1 (C151, C185) and high absorption (C180); amitriptyline high bidirectional rat intestinal Papp (C163, C176); zolmitriptan passive, non-saturable transport (C162, C173); hordenine high passive permeability with no detectable metabolism (C168); nortriptyline efflux ratio 1.37 (C165).",
      "card_ids": ["C151","C185","C180","C163","C176","C162","C173","C168","C165"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The only P-gp substrate record among relevant basic amines (fentanyl, C155/C200) shows high permeability and a low efflux ratio (1.24) with a 1.9-fold A-B increase on P-gp inhibition; this is mechanistic evidence of some efflux but not affirmative evidence of F < 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C155","C200"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "No L5 record provides affirmative evidence of F < 20% for the query or relevant analogs; the remaining unresolved component is hepatic first-pass/systemic clearance, not intestinal absorption or gut-wall efflux.",
      "card_ids": ["C17","C133","C151"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "gut_wall_efflux_intestinal_metabolism",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C151","C180","C185","C163","C176","C162","C173","C168","C165"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule.",
    "No direct query-specific Caco-2/permeability, efflux, or intestinal metabolism data exist; L5 records are for structurally related analogs.",
    "Hepatic first-pass metabolism and systemic clearance of the query are not directly measured; F could be lower than absorption if first-pass is extensive.",
    "The query is fully ionized at physiological pH (neutral fraction 0, logD 0.32), so formulation and dose effects on absorption are not directly tested.",
    "Species-dependent F for related molecules (e.g., alpidem 13% in male rat vs 32% in humans; proterguride 18% in monkey vs 62% in humans) limits quantitative transfer."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Prediction remains high. L5 gut-wall efflux/intestinal metabolism records for structurally related basic amines show high permeability and low efflux (imipramine ER 1.1, amitriptyline high Papp, zolmitriptan passive, hordenine high passive permeability), with no affirmative evidence of F < 20%. Combined with L1 human F outcomes >=20% for related basic amines and L4 high absorption evidence, F >= 20% is better supported; confidence remains high, with first-pass uncertainty expressed as evidence gaps."
}

